#. event 13 (justMoved)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0190"
msgid "I would not do that if I were you! "
msgstr ""

#. event 13 (justMoved)
msgctxt "bark 040F:01C6"
msgid "Stop! Thief! "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0590"
msgid "Hello. "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:060A"
msgid "I -do- wish that we had a larger house. "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0677"
msgid "Oh how I miss my baby boy. "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0701"
msgid "Do you need something? "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0740"
msgid "Very well then... "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:07A8"
msgid "We must clean up this house. "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:07F2"
msgid "I wonder what Cyrrus is doing right now? "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:084D"
msgid "No rats! "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:087F"
msgid "Mmmm, kith fillets! "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:08E7"
msgid "I truly despise rats! "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:091C"
msgid "I need some kith milk. "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0971"
msgid "I certainly am glad that a kith did not devour Cyrrus. "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0BE1"
msgid "Hello. "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0C56"
msgid "All day long, all I see are torax. "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0CC3"
msgid "Oh how I miss my baby boy. "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0D4D"
msgid "Do you need something? "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0D8C"
msgid "Very well then... "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0E07"
msgid "I wonder what the people in Tenebrae are doing? "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0E51"
msgid "I wonder what Cyrrus is doing right now? "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0EB6"
msgid "No rats! NO RATS!! "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0EF6"
msgid "I hope that no kiths come around. "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0F5E"
msgid "I truly despise rats! "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0F9C"
msgid "I need some variety in my life. "
msgstr ""

#. event 10 (enterFastArea)
msgctxt "bark 040F:0FEF"
msgid "I wish that Gwillim were more sensitive to my needs. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "bark 040F:1060"
msgid "Greetings "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "I -do- apologize, my lady. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Don't turn away from me, woman! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Hello, Corinth. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Hello, stranger. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "I hope I'm not intruding. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk))
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Goodbye. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Hello, stranger. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:1285"
msgid "Pardon me, sir, but I ask that you treat me with a bit more respect here upon my own land. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Hello, stranger. "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "I apologize, m'lady. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Hello, stranger. "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Quiet, woman! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I apologize, m'lady. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:13AB"
msgid "Apology accepted, sir. I hope that I was not too terse in my response. We certainly do not get many strangers up here. Allow me to introduce my self; I am Corinth. By what are you called? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I apologize, m'lady. "
#. sentence template: keep the {placeholders}
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "I'm called {name}."
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I apologize, m'lady. "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "I would rather not say. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Don't turn away from me, woman! "
msgctxt "bark 040F:146E"
msgid "What? I cannot believe how rude you are! Go away before I call the Tenebrae guards!! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Don't turn away from me, woman! "
#. sentence template: keep the {placeholders}
msgctxt "bark 040F:1519"
msgid "Well, I am pleased to meet you, {name}. You are welcome here."
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Don't turn away from me, woman! "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "So, you don't see many strangers? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Don't turn away from me, woman! "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Corinth? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Don't turn away from me, woman! "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "What do you do? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I would rather not say. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:15BE"
msgid "Very well, I shall not pry. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Quiet, woman! "
msgctxt "bark 040F:1665"
msgid "I will not tolerate such rudeness. Get off of my land, now! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Corinth? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:173C"
msgid "I was named for my mother who did not survive my birth. Father wished to preserve her memory by naming me after her. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Corinth? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Father "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Corinth? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Mother "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Mother "
msgctxt "bark 040F:17D2"
msgid "Did you not hear me? I said that my mother is dead. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Father "
msgctxt "bark 040F:1880"
msgid "Lleu was my father but he is dead now. Lleu was a fine herdsman but his devotion to his herd cost him dearly. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Father "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "He was a herdsman? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Father "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Cost him? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Father "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Lleu "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Lleu "
msgctxt "bark 040F:195B"
msgid "Yes, Lleu, it's an old name. It is rarely used today. In many ways my father's name suited him well. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Lleu "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Suited him? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Lleu "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "old name "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Suited him? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:1A03"
msgid "My father was an old fashioned man with old fashioned values. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Suited him? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Old values, huh? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Old values, huh? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:1B09"
msgid "Well I don't mean to say that we don't have values today. I certainly don't want you to get the impression that I'm not happy with our people's values. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Old values, huh? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "our people's values "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I -do- apologize, my lady. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:1BDD"
msgid "Very well, sir, I accept your apology. I am called Corinth. By what are you called? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Hello, Corinth. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:1C75"
msgid "Well, hello, my friend. I hope that all is well with you. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "old name "
msgctxt "bark 040F:1D11"
msgid "It is a very old name. But it's not a Zealan name. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "old name "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Zealan name? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Zealan name? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:1DB9"
msgid "That is what I was told. Actually, I know nothing about the Zealans. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Zealan name? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Who are the Zealans? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Who are the Zealans? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:1F62"
msgid "All I know of them are but dim memories of stories that I was told as a child. Supposedly there were a race of people that once lived here on Pagan who were quite savage. My father used to tell me that if I did not behave, the Zealans would come and get me. Anyway, that is all that I know of the Zealans. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "our people's values "
msgctxt "bark 040F:2021"
msgid "Lady Mordea has given us a culture to be proud of. Life is certainly better today than in the past. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "our people's values "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "the past "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "the past "
msgctxt "bark 040F:20C8"
msgid "Her Ladyship has given us peace and order. I am happy with that. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "He was a herdsman? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:2164"
msgid "Lleu was a herdsman from the time that he was a boy. It was all that he knew. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Cost him? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:21FB"
msgid "Yes, long ago Lleu's herd was attacked by a kith. The kith killed Lleu. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I hope I'm not intruding. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:22F6"
msgid "No, you are welcome here. Although you did alarm me a bit. We do no get many strangers up here. Still, it is not for simple folk to say where and when -you- travel. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I hope I'm not intruding. "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Do you know who I am? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Do you know who I am? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:2416"
msgid "Well, to be honest, no. But, someone of my stature certainly has no business telling a warrior what he can or can not do. But I have not introduced myself. I am Corinth. And by what are you called? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Do you know who I am? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "I prefer not to say. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I prefer not to say. "
#. sentence template: keep the {placeholders}
msgctxt "bark 040F:248D"
msgid "Well met, {name}. It is good to know you."
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I prefer not to say. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:253C"
msgid "Very well, I am sure that you have your reasons for your secrecy. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I prefer not to say. "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "You think I'm a warrior? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You think I'm a warrior? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:263E"
msgid "Come now, do not be modest. You have the obvious look of a warrior. Look how you are dressed! I may live in the country, but I am not stupid. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What do you do? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:2718"
msgid "As we live in the country, away from most people, I do many things. Since my son did move away I am not as busy as I once was. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What do you do? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Many things "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What do you do? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Your son? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Many things "
msgctxt "bark 040F:2811"
msgid "I take care of my husband, feed him, stitch his clothes and such. I also keep the house and help tend the torax from time to time. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Many things "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Your husband? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Many things "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Torax? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Your son? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:28EF"
msgid "My dear Cyrrus. I am so proud of him. His father and I are but simple people. But Cyrrus will do great things. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Your son? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "His father? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Your son? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Great things? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Your son? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Simple folk. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "His father? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:297B"
msgid "That would be my husband, Gwillim. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Simple folk. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:2AAC"
msgid "Look about you, my lord. Does this look like the home of a wealthy family? Ours are not easy lives, yet we are proud people. Not many can do what we do. And our family has lived in this valley and worked the land for generations. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Simple folk. "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "You've been here for generations? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You've been here for generations? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:2BFA"
msgid "Oh yes. There used to be a great many families that lived in the valley. But that was long ago. Now, only Gwillim and I are left to keep the legacy of the valley alive. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You've been here for generations? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Legacy? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You've been here for generations? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "What happened to the others? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Legacy? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:2D24"
msgid "Yes, we are the only folk that are left who know the myths and legends of the valley. It is sad, but we are the only people left who care of such things. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Legacy? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "No one cares? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "No one cares? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:2E09"
msgid "There is no one -left- to care. Roam this valley all that you wish and the only people that you will see are Gwillim and myself. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What happened to the others? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:2F2D"
msgid "Well, there was a great war long, long ago. That was the beginning of the end, I suppose. Since that time, many people believed that the land was cursed. Many people died and many others moved away. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What happened to the others? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Cursed? By a ghost, perhaps? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What happened to the others? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Cursed? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What happened to the others? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Where did the people move? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Cursed? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:3095"
msgid "Well that is what some folk believe, but Gwillim and I... That is to say, ahh... Some people believe that the land is cursed. It is best left at that. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where did the people move? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:311E"
msgid "My father says that most of them moved to the city. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where did the people move? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "This was before your time? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where did the people move? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "The city? You're kidding! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "The city? You're kidding! "
msgctxt "bark 040F:322B"
msgid "No, I am quite serious. The city, like the valley has suffered much and many people have died. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "This was before your time? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:3323"
msgid "Oh yes, it was long ago. I have only heard stories. By the time I was born, there were only two families here in the valley, mine and Gwillim's. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "This was before your time? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "What about when you go? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "This was before your time? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "And Gwillim's family? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "And Gwillim's family? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:3434"
msgid "Oh, they too died off. Gwillim's only brother died rather tragically, and his parents eventually died of age. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "And Gwillim's family? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "How did he die? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Cursed? By a ghost, perhaps? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:34DA"
msgid "Yes! How did you know that? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Cursed? By a ghost, perhaps? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "I have heard tales. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Cursed? By a ghost, perhaps? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Can you tell me of the ghost? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What about when you go? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:35D4"
msgid "It is sad, but I fear that when Gwillim and I are gone, then gone too shall be this way of life. I blame myself for it. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What about when you go? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "That is sad, indeed. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What about when you go? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "You blame -yourself-? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "That is sad, indeed. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:36CB"
msgid "I suppose that is the way of things. But still, I can not help but cry when I think of it. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You blame -yourself-? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:37D3"
msgid "Oh, please forget that ever I said such a thing. I need not trouble someone who is a virtual stranger with talk such as this. I have rattled on for far too long as it is. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You blame -yourself-? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "This is no trouble. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You blame -yourself-? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "How could you blame yourself? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "This is no trouble. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:3898"
msgid "I thank you. You are kind to say so. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "How could you blame yourself? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:3990"
msgid "Well, there was an accident many years ago... You see, Cyrrus was not our only child. Oh dear, I can not believe that I am telling you all of this. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "How could you blame yourself? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "It's ok, go on. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "How could you blame yourself? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Stop if you wish. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Stop if you wish. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:3B65"
msgid "No, I will continue. For some reason it feels good to tell this to someone. I had a child after Cyrrus, a baby girl. One day while the baby was still very young, I went into the barn to fetch a pail. I was only gone but for a moment, but while I was out of the house, a kith did come into the house and devour my baby. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Stop if you wish. "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "How tragic! "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "It's ok, go on. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:3CEE"
msgid "Yes, I shall. You see, when Cyrrus was still young, I gave birth to a baby girl. One day while the baby was still very young, I went into the barn to fetch a pale. I was only gone but for a moment, but while I was out of the house, a kith did come into the house and devour my baby. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "How tragic! "
msgctxt "bark 040F:3E4A"
msgid "For years I have carried the shame and guilt of knowing that I was responsible for my baby's death. Gwillim has always been very kind and supportive. He tried to tell me that it was not my fault, yet always will have to live with this sadness. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I have heard tales. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:3EDC"
msgid "Strange. I had no idea that such tales have stretched very far. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Can you tell me of the ghost? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:3FE3"
msgid "Well, I have not seen the ghost myself. I have only heard stories. However, Gwillim, my husband, has seen the creature, but he is very reluctant to talk about it. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Can you tell me of the ghost? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Gwillim's seen the ghost? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Can you tell me of the ghost? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Why is he reluctant to talk? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Gwillim's seen the ghost? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:4151"
msgid "Yes, twice, and it was long ago. The first time was when he and his brother were young men. They where watching over their herd when upon the hillside they saw a glowing form above them. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Gwillim's seen the ghost? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "What about the second time? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Gwillim's seen the ghost? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "They both saw it? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What about the second time? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:42D2"
msgid "The second time, the ghost was actually on the ground, in front of Gwillim. He said that the ghost appeared to dance around him, as though it was mocking Gwillim. He also said that it looked most unusual for a ghost. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What about the second time? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Where was it the second time? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What about the second time? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "It looked unusual? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "They both saw it? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:43E4"
msgid "Indeed they did. From that time on, Karpese, that was Gwillim's brother was obsessed with capturing the ghost. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Why is he reluctant to talk? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:4532"
msgid "Gwillim was frightened very deeply by what he saw. He is a strong man and does not scare easily. Whatever Gwillim saw did disturb him deeply and brings back memories of his brother. Therefore Gwillim does not like to speak of the ghost. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "It looked unusual? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:46B3"
msgid "Yes. Anyone who has had the misfortune to have visited the graveyard has probably seen a ghost floating in the distance. It is not unusual to see something such as that in a place where there is nothing but death. But Gwillim told me that the ghost that haunts this valley is different. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "It looked unusual? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "How is it different? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "How is it different? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:47E0"
msgid "Well, most ghosts that people have seen are vaporous in appearance. According to Gwillim, this ghost here is invisible except for the armor which it bears. It is most unusual. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Where was it the second time? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:4898"
msgid "I am not certain. Gwillim could tell you if you can get him to speak of the ghost. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "How did he die? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:492E"
msgid "He went searching for the ghost and did never return. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Torax? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:4A4D"
msgid "Yes, the animals that you will see grazing here in the valley. Do not tell me that you have never heard of a torax. We have been trying to increase the size of our herd so that we can save a little bit more money. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Torax? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Save money? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Save money? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:4B21"
msgid "Yes, it is difficult to do because we don't have very much. Sometimes my husband hunts kiths to bring in extra food. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Save money? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "He hunts kiths? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "He hunts kiths? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:4C01"
msgid "Kith meat is very tasty but they are dangerous animals. It is said that a kith can cut a man in half with its jaws. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "He hunts kiths? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "That sounds dangerous. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "That sounds dangerous. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:4CBA"
msgid "Not many people hunt them. But Gwillim is very good at it. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Your husband? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:4D47"
msgid "Gwillim is my husband. He is a strong and goodly man. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Your husband? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Strong and goodly? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Strong and goodly? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:4E42"
msgid "Many men drink every night and beat their wives but Gwillim does not do such things. He does not even mind that I sacrifice to Hydros. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Strong and goodly? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "You sacrifice to Hydros? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You sacrifice to Hydros? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:4F46"
msgid "Gwillim is a farmer, so he sacrifices to Lithos, the Earth Titan. But, like my father, I sacrifice to the Water Titan, Hydros. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "You sacrifice to Hydros? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Why Hydros? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Why Hydros? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:5036"
msgid "My father taught me to sacrifice to Hydros. All of my family has sacrificed to the Lurker for as far back as any can remember. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Great things? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:50DE"
msgid "Yes! Cyrrus has gone to study with the Theurgists. He will help many people as a Theurgist. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Great things? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Theurgist "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Great things? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Help people? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Theurgist "
msgctxt "bark 040F:51BD"
msgid "The Theurgists are the disciples of the Air Titan. Although Gwillim sacrifices to Lithos, I believe that Cyrrus was born to be a Theurgist. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Theurgist "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "But what of Hydros? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Theurgist "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Born to be a Theurgist? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Help people? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:52A4"
msgid "The Theurgists specialize in healing the sick. Some say that they can even bring back the dead. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "But what of Hydros? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:53C4"
msgid "All of the Titans are worthy of service. Gwillim did not much like the idea of Cyrrus being a Theurgist but saw the boy's dedication. If Cyrrus is meant to serve Stratos then we must not stand in his way. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "But what of Hydros? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "All of the Titans are worthy? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "All of the Titans are worthy? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:5517"
msgid "By that, I mean that all of the Titans are great powers. I do not mean to say that all are not worthy of good people's service. I would not claim that Pyros and his sorcerers are worthy of such. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "All of the Titans are worthy? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Sorcerers? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Born to be a Theurgist? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:569C"
msgid "All of his life Cyrrus has most enjoyed caring for others. He has always a talent for healing. It did not matter if it was a person or an animal, Cyrrus would heal it if it were sick. I knew that he was born to be a Theurgist, not to spend his life on a farm. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Born to be a Theurgist? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Even animals? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Born to be a Theurgist? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "Not at the farm "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Sorcerers? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:5767"
msgid "Ask me nothing of them. It is ill business to speak of the sorcerers. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Not at the farm "
msgctxt "bark 040F:5854"
msgid "Gwillim wanted very much for Cyrrus to follow in his footsteps at the farm. I convinced Cyrrus that his future was more important than his father's traditions. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Not at the farm "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "His future? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Not at the farm "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "His father's tradition. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "His father's tradition. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:599B"
msgid "All of Gwillim's kin have always been herdsmen. Gwillim takes great pride in working the land. As Cyrrus is our only son, Gwillim expected Cyrrus to carry on the family's traditions. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "So, you don't see many strangers? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:5A6F"
msgid "We rarely have visitors here in the country.\tWe do see that strange old hermit once in a while, though. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "So, you don't see many strangers? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "What hermit? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What hermit? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:5B8F"
msgid "I believe that his name is Mythran. He goes into Tenebrae now and then, for supplies I suppose. No one knows much about Mythran but there are many tales about him. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What hermit? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "What kinds of tales? "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "What kinds of tales? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:5CC1"
msgid "Oh I don't not know them all. People claim that he knows magic. Some people even claim to have bought magic scrolls from the old hermit. But I would not believe everything that you hear. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "His future? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:5E09"
msgid "I knew that if Cyrrus became a farmer, he would be poor for the rest of life. Gwillim does not know that I convinced Cyrrus to seek the Theurgists, but I had to, for Cyrrus' sake. Now he can lead a life far richer than that of a farm man. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Even animals? "
msgctxt "bark 040F:5EB8"
msgid "My, but you do ask many questions! But yes, Cyrrus loves animals. He has always been a caring man. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Even animals? "
msgctxt "ask 040F"
msgid "I'm sorry if I ask too many questions. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "I'm sorry if I ask too many questions. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:5FE9"
msgid "No, I am sorry if I made you uncomfortable. I enjoy your company! As I said, we do not see many visitors here, I am glad to have someone to talk to. "
msgstr ""

#. event 01 (use (talk)), after "Goodbye. "
msgctxt "bark 040F:6054"
msgid "Farewell "
msgstr ""
